From 5b5b95e1fd8944367f4375479eb372fa993a4483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:48:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] defers: continuation on failure (zig/go doctrine) - a
 failing defer no longer halts the chain

- run_pending_defers: a failing thunk no longer nils the rest of the range.
  the remaining defers run; the FIRST failure's error is what propagates.
  the failing thunk's own callees are torn down with THEIR defers run.
- the chronology marker: an in-flight error that passed through a defer
  thunk frame IS a defer failure - it is the chain's first, later failures
  drop against it instead of replacing it. an original error stays
  replaceable by the first failing defer (the documented replacement rule).
- defer_cascade flag + its nil lane removed; the thunk frame flag is now
  the marker. first-error accounting (capture/restore of the error lane)
  rides a gc guard across the rest of the chain.
- deferr rides the same lanes (one tag, compile-time distinction only).
- oom stays the stop-everything lane.
- tests: defer_cascade.ok (the old halt semantics) replaced by
  defer_continuation.ok + defer_continuation_uncaught.ok +
  coros/defers_continuation.ok (R22 death sweep + continuation).
  425/425 on plain, threaded, asan, aggressive-gc.
